claim.claim-text:
1. A system for signal identification in a radiofrequency (RF) environment, comprising:
at least one node device including a processor and memory;
wherein the at least one node device is in communication with at least one artificial intelligence (AI) engine;
wherein the at least one node device is operable to receive RF data based on the RF environment;
wherein the at least one node device is operable to average Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) data derived from the RF data into at least one tile;
wherein the at least one AI engine is operable to generate an output for the at least one tile to identify at least one signal;
wherein the at least one tile is represented as at least one waterfall image; and
wherein location information for the at least one signal is displayed on at least one user interface as at least one line of bearing.

10. An apparatus for signal identification in a radiofrequency (RF) environment, comprising:
a node device including a processor and memory;
wherein the node device is in communication with at least one artificial intelligence (AI) engine;
wherein the node device is operable to receive RF data;
wherein the node device is operable to average Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) data derived from the RF data into at least one tile;
wherein the at least one AI engine is operable to generate an output for the at least one tile to identify and correspond at least one signal with a probability;
wherein the at least one tile is represented as at least one waterfall image; and
wherein at least one line of bearing is displayed for the at least one signal on at least one user interface.

16. A method for signal analysis in a radiofrequency (RF) environment, comprising:
at least one node device receiving Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) data derived from RF data based on the RF environment;
averaging the FFT data by the at least one node device into at least one tile and representing the at least one tile as at least one waterfall image;
generating an output for the at least one tile by at least one artificial intelligence (AI) engine in communication with the at least one node device to identify and correlate at least one signal with a probability;
classifying at least one signal emitting device by comparing the at least one signal emitted from the at least one signal emitting device to classification data stored in a classification library; and
displaying at least one line of bearing for the at least one signal on at least one user interface.
